{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 8, :comments ["<b>You shall open</b> — peh doubled, to say: open your hand and also your mouth to entreat him with words. Another interpretation: one worthy of bread, give him bread; one worthy of delicacies, give him delicacies, and provide him with every kind of sweetness. Another interpretation: פתח תפתח — if he is embarrassed, bring it to his doorway. Another interpretation: פתח תפתח — the matter is doubled, and likewise נתון תתן לו, העניק תעניק לו — to say there is no measure to the gift, rather you give and give again." "<b>פתח</b> — defective vav; a commandment on the sixth day to give bread to the poor, from the enactment of Ezra." "<b>פתח</b> — three times in the Masorah: two in this matter, and the other פתוח נפתחו שערי ארצך. This teaches that if you open your hand to him, the gates of heaven will open for you so that your prayer is accepted, and if not, they will not open for you, as stated: אוטם אזנו מזעקת דל וגו'." "<b>די מחסרו אשר יחסר</b> — rashei tevot: דמאי — what do we feed the poor? דמאי."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 15, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-12T19:09:49.038571072Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}